  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: 'How much does shed shelving cost?', a: 'Built-in utility shelving runs $45 to $70 per linear foot for one tier, up to $85 to $130 for three tiers. A 6 to 10 foot utility storage wall is $900 to $1,600 or more.' },
    { q: 'How deep should shed shelves be?', a: '12 to 16 inches for general storage, 20 to 24 inches for large totes, and 24 to 30 inches for a workbench.' },
    { q: 'How tall should a workbench be?', a: 'It depends on the user and the task. Standing woodworking benches often fall in the mid-30-inch range, but Appalachian Sheds sets the height for the person who will use it.' },
  ],
  ctaTitle: 'Plan Your Storage Layout With Edwin',
};
---
<OptionPage page={page} />
